      "content": "okay that's definitely better and looks more professional. the score is getting closer to where we need it to be. \n\none thing though—the reviewer is still being a bit picky. it's specifically looking for more granularity in the steps. it wants to see more \"navigational landmarks\" throughout the document. \n\ncan you do one more pass? try to expand the sections so there's more to click through. maybe break down the \"Authentication\" or \"Making Requests\" into even smaller sub-steps or subsections. i really don't want it to become a wall of text, but if we can get more headings and bullets in there it should pass the check. just keep the info accurate!",
